  "story": "105 research teams analysed this dataset; 68 found that the religiosity-well-being relation grows with perceived cultural norms with an interval above zero. The default analysis gives interaction beta = 0.045 (95% CI 0.026 to 0.063), p < 0.001, n = 10,535. The verdict changes in 1 of 15 universes; the nearest is Pooled OLS, robust errors: interaction beta = 0.018 (95% CI -0.000 to 0.037), p = 0.056, n = 10,535.",
  "column_notes": {
    "country": "country of the respondent (24 countries); one of the 24 countries of the MARP survey",
    "rel_1": "religiosity questionnaire item 1 of 9; the nine rel_* items form the religiosity scale",
    "cnorm_1": "perceived cultural norm of religion, item 1 of 2 (the respondent's own perception)",
    "cnorm_2": "perceived cultural norm of religion, item 2 of 2 (the respondent's own perception)",
    "wb_gen_1": "general well-being item 1 of 2",
    "wb_gen_2": "general well-being item 2 of 2",
    "wb_phys_1": "physical well-being item 1 of 7; the wb_phys_* items feed wb_phys_mean",
    "wb_psych_1": "psychological well-being item 1 of 6; the wb_psych_* items feed wb_psych_mean",
    "wb_soc_1": "social well-being item 1 of 3; the wb_soc_* items feed wb_soc_mean",
    "wb_overall_mean": "raw column already in the data: the 18-item composite mean of overall well-being; no step needs to create it",
    "wb_phys_mean": "raw column already in the data: mean of the physical well-being items",
    "wb_psych_mean": "raw column already in the data: mean of the psychological well-being items",
    "wb_soc_mean": "raw column already in the data: mean of the social well-being items",
    "age": "age of the respondent in years",
    "gender": "gender of the respondent (categorical)",
    "ses": "self-reported socio-economic status of the respondent (numeric)",
    "education": "education level of the respondent (numeric)",
    "gdp_scaled": "scaled GDP of the respondent's country; constant within a country",
    "attention_check": "answer code for the survey attention check: 1 means the respondent passed; any other value (2 to 7) means they failed",
    "rel_2": "religiosity questionnaire item 2 of 9; the nine rel_* items form the religiosity scale",
    "rel_3": "religiosity questionnaire item 3 of 9; the nine rel_* items form the religiosity scale",
